00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.100
on AI and semiconductor strength.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.100
One practical way to implement this idea

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:08.060
is to allocate a sleeve of a TFSA or RRSP

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.980
to a broad Asia-X China ETF

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.280
or to individual holdings in Japanese

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.020
and Taiwanese semiconductor supply chain names.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.320
Rebalance the sleeve quarterly

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.020
using the 200-day moving average as a guide.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:25.960
This approach worked best during the 2015 to 2016 China slowdown

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.840
and the 2022 global rate hike cycle

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.240
when markets with clear policy predictability outperformed.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.020
The main risks are currency fluctuation

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:38.020
and slower overall GDP growth in the region,

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.360
so keep the position under 10% of the equity sleeve.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.280
That geographic approach pairs naturally

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.400
with today's investor education topic

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.420
on how stagflation changes central bank behavior.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:53.360
Imagine you added a broad equity ETF last month

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.040
expecting the new Fed chair to cut rates on any growth slowdown,

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.100
only to watch the 10-year yield spike instead

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.680
because inflation and weak growth arrived together.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.660
The mechanism runs through the Fed's dual mandate.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.680
When consumer spending edges up only marginally

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:11.060
while the saving rate hits a four-year low

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.420
and war-driven price pressures persist,

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.280
the central bank faces a credibility test

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.940
because traditional rate cuts would fuel inflation

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:19.460
further.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.340
Professionals always check the personal consumption expenditures

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.120
deflator and the saving rate before assuming policy easing.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.460
Those two data points together determine whether the Fed

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.820
can ease without breaking its inflation target.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.700
The biggest mistake with stagflation setups

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:39.000
is assuming the Fed will prioritize growth over price stability

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:40.780
the way it did in 2020.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.700
Instead, always model two scenarios,

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.920
one with 50 basis point cuts and one with hikes

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.360
before sizing any duration or growth stock exposure.

